@startuml requirement-issue-states
' cumin works - states of a requirement issue.
' A state is a label on GitHub. "do /" in a state says what goes on while the issue has the label.
' A transition is written as in UML: trigger [guard] / effect. The row of issue-states.md stands in
' parentheses at the end.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "Draft (no status label)" as Draft
Draft : do / the Owner writes the requirement

state "cumin/status/ready" as Ready
Ready : do / wait for a free slot

state "cumin/status/planning" as Planning
Planning : do / the Planner splits the requirement

state "cumin/status/awaiting-owner-review (sub-issues)" as PlanReview
PlanReview : do / the Owner checks the sub-issues

state "cumin/status/implementing" as Implementing
Implementing : do / the sub-issues are worked on
Implementing : every sub-issue closed [no acceptance check yet]
Implementing :   / request the acceptance check (R4)

state "cumin/status/awaiting-owner-review (acceptance)" as Acceptance
Acceptance : do / the Owner decides the acceptance

state "cumin/status/awaiting-owner-decision" as Decision
Decision : do / the Owner answers

[*] --> Draft
Draft --> Ready : the Owner adds cumin/status/ready
Draft --> Implementing : ready added to a sub-issue (R3)
Ready --> Planning : poll [ready is the Owner's,\nblockers closed, slot free]\n/ request the split (R1)
Planning --> PlanReview : Planner run ended\n[split verified]\n/ notify the Owner (R2)
Planning --> Implementing : Planner run ended\n[every sub-issue closed] (R2)
Planning --> Decision : Planner run ended\n[split not verified, or blocked]\n/ write the reason, notify the Owner (R2)
PlanReview --> Implementing : ready added to a sub-issue (R3)
Implementing --> Acceptance : acceptance check written\n/ notify the Owner (R7)
Implementing --> Decision : Planner run ended [blocked]\n/ post the question, notify the Owner (R4)
Implementing --> PlanReview : only sub-issues without\na status label remain\n/ notify the Owner (R6)
Acceptance --> Implementing : ready added to a sub-issue (R3)
Acceptance --> [*] : the Owner closes the issue (R5)
Decision --> Ready : the Owner adds cumin/status/ready

legend right
  A box is a state: a label on GitHub. "do /" is what goes on in the state.
  An arrow is a transition: trigger [guard] / effect.
  The line without "do /" inside cumin/status/implementing is an internal transition: the label stays.
  In parentheses: the row of issue-states.md today.
endlegend

@enduml
